# Complements on the small pro-étale site

The small pro-étale site `X.ProEt` of a scheme is the category of schemes weakly étale over
`X`, topologized by the pro-étale topology `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.topology`, which
is generated by the precoverage of quasi-compact jointly surjective families of weakly étale
morphisms. In contrast to the small étale site, a covering is *not* merely a jointly
surjective family: quasi-compactness is part of the condition, so the covering criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff` has no analogue here and the
inputs below are phrased in terms of membership in `proetalePrecoverage` instead.

This file provides the site-theoretic inputs for the pro-étale six functors of the
`WeilConjectures.SixFunctors.ProEtale` folder, in the same roles as
`WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.Small` and
`WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.Etale` play for the étale ones.

## Main results

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.mem_topology_iff`: a sieve is covering for the pro-étale
  topology exactly when it contains a presieve of the pro-étale precoverage. This is
  `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition` for the
  small pro-étale site, and it is what makes the covering conditions below checkable.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.isContinuous_overPullback`: base change along an
  *arbitrary* morphism `g : W ⟶ U` is continuous for the pro-étale topologies. It preserves
  covers because the base change square of `MorphismProperty.Over.isPullback_map_left` is
  cartesian and `proetalePrecoverage` is stable under base change, and it preserves
  compatible families because it is representably flat, the small pro-étale site being
  finitely complete.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.isContinuous_overMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.isCocontinuous_overMap`: the localization functor
  `MorphismProperty.Over.map ⊤ h` along a weakly étale `f : V ⟶ U` is continuous and
  cocontinuous. Both directions are essentially a reindexing: the localization functor is
  the identity on underlying schemes and morphisms.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.ofArrows_baseChange_mem_topology`: the base changes
  `V ×_X W i` of a pro-étale covering family `g i : W i ⟶ X` cover every `V : X.ProEt`.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.isTerminalSectionsOfIsEmpty`: a sheaf on the small
  pro-étale site has terminal sections over an object whose underlying scheme is empty.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage_le_proetalePrecoverage`: a Zariski open cover
  is a pro-étale covering family. This is what makes the two-open cover of
  `WeilConjectures.SixFunctors.ProEtale.FiniteCoefficient.LowerShriek.Proper` available.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.mem_topology_of_openImmersion`: a sieve on `U : X.ProEt`
  containing a jointly surjective family of open immersions `Y i ⟶ U`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.ofOpenImmersionHom`) is covering.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.toProEt`: the inclusion `ν : X.Etale ⥤ X.ProEt` of the small
  étale site into the small pro-étale site, which is fully faithful, representably flat and
  continuous (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isContinuous_toProEt`).

-/

